# Backend deployment — Symply Ecosystem

When deploying **shared Worker** changes (same `src/index.ts`, all brand wrangler configs), deploy the full fleet — staging all brands, then production all brands. **Only from the `main` checkout.** Never from an `<app>-v2` clone (`documents/ecosystem/BRANCHING.md`).

```bash
eval "$(./scripts/secrets/export-env.sh)"
cd backend
npm run deploy:fleet
```

**House-only** (default wrangler.toml, no `-c`):

```bash
npm run deploy:house:all
# deprecated alias: npm run deploy:all
```

Rapid-development policy: agents may run this **without asking** — **from the `main` checkout only**. Never `deploy:fleet` from an `<app>-v2` clone. Shared backend lands on `main` (flagged off if unfinished). See `documents/ecosystem/BRANCHING.md`.

