## Per-brand (when only one Worker changed)

```bash
eval "$(./scripts/secrets/export-env.sh)"
cd backend
npm run deploy:house:all      # or deploy:budget:all / deploy:kaizen:all / deploy:health:all
```

**Language** uses separate `backend-language/` — `npm run deploy:language:all` (not part of `deploy:fleet`).

Rapid-development policy: agents may run this **without asking** — from the `main` checkout only. Never from an `<app>-v2` clone.

- Mobile dev → **staging** API (per brand Worker)
- Cron-limit warning on production deploy can be ignored if Version ID updates
- Separate D1 / R2 / KV per env — run migrations for **both** envs when schema changes
- House, Budget, Kaizen, and Health are **separate** backends — migrate account data with `migrate:house-to-budget` / `migrate:house-to-kaizen`
- Health D1 migrate: `db:migrate:health:*` runs `refuse-health-0092.sh` (blocks while `0092_*` migration exists unless `HEALTH_ALLOW_0092=1`)

See `documents/ecosystem/SERVICES.md` and `AGENTS.md`.
